1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,830
Okay so you decided to officially transform yourself and your life congratulations I'm so proud of you.
好，你决定正式改变自己和生活了，恭喜，我真为你骄傲。

2
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:11,040
Now we need to take our first step so your first step starts with you figuring out where your starting line is.
现在要迈出第一步：先弄清楚自己的起跑线在哪里。

3
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:16,280
So where you're at currently and your finish line which is where you want to be the best version of yourself.
也就是你现在的位置，以及终点——你想成为的、最好的自己。

4
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:21,520
So I want you guys to pull out your journal your notes app a piece of paper write it in the comments below.
所以，请拿出日记、备忘录、一张纸，或者写在下面的评论里。

5
00:00:21,520 --> 00:00:29,870
Literally anything where you can document it do it the first one is envision the best version of yourself what habits goals and thoughts align with that version.
总之找个能记录的地方去做。第一，想象最好的自己，哪些习惯、目标和想法与之相符？

6
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:35,600
Second what current habits are hindering you from becoming the best version of yourself so answer those two questions.
第二，目前哪些习惯阻碍你成为最好的自己？回答这两个问题。

7
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:38,160
Next take stock of what you already have.
接下来，盘点你已经拥有的东西。

8
00:00:38,160 --> 00:00:42,040
So as you prepare to create this new version of yourself the best version of yourself.
在你准备创造这个全新的、更好的自己时，

9
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:47,440
It's really important that you take stock of what you already have and like what you already got going on if you know what I mean.
盘点已有的东西，以及正在做的事情，很重要，你懂我的意思吧。

10
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:53,840
Cuz honestly it's so inspiring to know what great habits that you actually do have that you didn't even realize or give credit to yourself for.
因为发现自己已有却没意识到、也没肯定过的好习惯，其实很鼓舞人。

11
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:57,840
So write down and answer these two lists five good habits I've always had.
所以，把这两份清单写下来：五个我一直都有的好习惯。

12
00:00:57,840 --> 00:01:03,520
So these are going to be habits that you already have and you practice but you don't remember consciously creating it if that makes sense.
这些是你已经拥有并践行、却不记得有意识培养过的习惯，明白我的意思吗？

13
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:09,160
And then five intentionally created habits so good habits that you have set for yourself and that you successfully do.
然后是五个刻意培养的习惯：你为自己设定并确实做到的好习惯。

14
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:15,550
And listen you might have some trouble at first thinking of good habits that you actually have cuz you think that you're like the worst person in the world.
听着，一开始你也许想不出自己的好习惯，因为你可能觉得自己糟糕透了。

15
00:01:15,560 --> 00:01:20,079
That's genuinely what I thought before because I had such low self esteem but that is not true.
以前我真这么想过，因为我自尊心很低，但这并不是真的。

16
00:01:20,079 --> 00:01:28,320
I do not care how down bad you are right now or how awful you think you are as a person everybody has some sort of good habit that they already practice.
无论你现在多低落、觉得自己多差，每个人总已有一些正在践行的好习惯。

17
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:32,640
So really sit there brainstorm think hard and be kind to yourself okay.
所以，真的坐下来想一想、认真动动脑，也对自己温柔一点，好吗？

18
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:41,310
So for example for me five good habits I've always had making my bed every morning always saying please and thank you showing gratitude always positively encouraging others.
以我为例，我一直有的五个好习惯包括：早上叠床、常说请和谢谢、表达感激、积极鼓励别人。

19
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:47,000
Being a good listener and friend under five intentionally created habits quit drinking alcohol I do not drink anymore.
还有做一个善于倾听的朋友。刻意培养的五个习惯则包括戒酒；我现在不喝酒了。

20
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:52,750
Hydrating every morning before my coffee being more organized with my schedule and creating to dos for myself.
每天喝咖啡前先补水，更有条理地安排日程，并为自己列待办事项。

21
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:57,320
Being healed and emotionally available very important and then waking up early.
还有她所说的疗愈自己、在情感上愿意投入，这很重要；以及早起。

22
00:01:57,320 --> 00:02:03,400
So research actually shows that in order for us to actually stick to a good habit and stick to a goal that we want.
作者接着说，研究表明，要坚持一个好习惯、坚持一个想实现的目标，

23
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:07,200
We need to inherently believe that we have the ability to change.
就需要从内心相信自己有改变的能力。

24
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:13,560
So believe it or not you already have proof of this already through this list and it could be the smallest of habits it does not matter.
所以，信不信由你，这份清单已经是证明。哪怕是最小的习惯，也没关系。

25
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:21,280
We all have inherent proof within ourselves that we have the ability to change and transform and be able to accomplish anything that we set our minds to.
我们每个人都能从自身找到这种证据：有能力改变，并完成自己下定决心要做的事。

26
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:26,880
So this amazing advice is not from me okay I got it from this self help book it's called badass habits by jen sincero.
这个建议并不是我原创的，我从一本自助书中读到，书名和作者为自动识别，待原声核对。

27
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:32,270
I've shouted out this book so many times I can't even count but I'm going to continue to shout it out because it is that good.
我推荐过这本书很多次，数都数不清，但还会继续推荐，因为我觉得它很好。

28
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:39,040
This is genuinely one of the best self help books I've ever read and I've read a lot and a lot of them are really boring okay.
这是我读过最好的自助书之一，我读过很多，其中不少让我觉得很无聊。

29
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:43,000
But this one is genuinely entertaining like I was audibly laughing reading this.
但这本书很有趣，我读的时候真的笑出了声。

30
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:49,440
So the author talks all about how to actually stick to good habits and how to achieve goals for yourself in a very realistic way.
作者以很实际的方式，谈怎样坚持好习惯、实现自己的目标。

31
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:54,520
I'm telling you I've been able to create and stick to so many good habits because of this book right here.
我告诉你们，因为这本书，我得以养成并坚持了不少好习惯。

32
00:02:54,520 --> 00:03:00,320
She does such a great job of explaining why you should strive to be the best version of yourself and she is so real in this book too.
她很会解释为什么要努力成为更好的自己，而且书中也很坦诚。

33
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:06,320
She talks about how she was dead broke before how she had a smoking problem and how she transformed from that and I love that for her.
她说自己曾经身无分文、有吸烟问题，后来改变了，我真替她高兴。
